# TERRA — environment configuration
#
# TERRA runs with NO keys out of the box. The globe, place search, earthquakes
# (USGS), weather alerts (NOAA/NWS), satellites (CelesTrak), and the free
# high-detail base maps (Satellite = Esri World Imagery, Streets = OpenStreetMap)
# all work with no credentials.
#
# The keys below are OPTIONAL and only unlock extra detail. Copy this file to
# `.env` and fill in what you want. VITE_* values are bundled into the public
# client, so only put keys here that are safe to expose in a browser app (all of
# the below are browser-side keys; restrict them by HTTP referrer in the
# provider's console). NEVER put a private/server secret behind a VITE_ prefix.

# ── Cesium Ion (free tier) — unlocks 3D terrain + 3D buildings ────────────────
# Where: sign in at https://ion.cesium.com/  → "Access Tokens" → copy the
# default token (or make a new one). Free tier is generous for personal use.
# Enables the "3D terrain" and "3D buildings" toggles in Settings.
VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# ── Google Maps Platform — unlocks Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles ─────────────
# This is the real "like Google Earth" 3D (textured buildings + terrain).
# Where: https://console.cloud.google.com/  → create/select a project → enable
# the "Map Tiles API" → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create API key. Then
# restrict the key (HTTP referrers) so it can't be abused. Google's Map Tiles
# API has a monthly free allowance; usage beyond it is billed, so keep the key
# restricted. Once set, choose Base map → "Google 3D".
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the geocoding endpoint (default: Open-Meteo, no key).
# VITE_GEOCODE_BASE_URL=https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1
